<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Dalmatia</h1><p class="st-meta">1815 CE – 1918 CE · capital Zara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Austrian crown land along the Adriatic coast, where Croatian and Italian national movements competed for a century before it joined Yugoslavia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> had taken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetian-dalmatia">Venetian Dalmatia</a> in 1797 but lost it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> it recovered the coast, now including the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-ragusa">Republic of Ragusa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-kotor">Bay of Kotor</a>, and organised it in 1815 as the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, a crown land of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zara</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> was poor and rural, living from wine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a>, fishing and seafaring, and many emigrated to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. Its diet, created in 1861, was at first dominated by the Italian-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/autonomist-party-dalmatia">Autonomist Party</a>, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-party-dalmatia">Croatian People's Party</a> won control in 1870. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> sought union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-croatia-slavonia">Croatia-Slavonia</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> refused. The Austrian navy defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lissa-1866">Lissa</a> in 1866.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In October 1918 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-slovenes-croats-and-serbs">State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs</a>, and then the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zara</a> and some islands passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rapallo-1920">Treaty of Rapallo</a> in 1920, returning to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> after 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-dalmatia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Dalmatia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: DIREKTOR · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Dalmatia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1815 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Franz Joseph I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Croatian, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dalmatia (Austrian), Königreich Dalmatien</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1866&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dalmatia" aria-label="Kingdom of Dalmatia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5045 616 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Dalmatia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5365 872L5343 812M5365 872L5381 747M5365 872L5380 747M5365 872L5378 819"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5343 812h0M5381 747h0M5380 7